# Descriptor: [anti-B0 -> X(D_s K) l- nu] dummy-resonant gap mode, e and mu, cc
# NickName: B0_DsKlnu_dummyres_gapmodes
# Documentation: B0 -> D_s K l nu via wide dummy resonance (m=2.8 GeV, w=3.0 GeV), isospin
#   partner of decfiles/gap_modes/Bplus/DsKenu (B+ -> D_s- K+ l+ nu). Confirmed nonzero per
#   arXiv:2605.03021 (Eqs. 5-8): the paper derives B(B0 -> Ds(*)-K0 l+ nu) = (5.63+-0.88)e-4
#   from the measured B(B+ -> Ds(*)-K+ l+ nu) = (6.06+-0.95)e-4 via isospin symmetry and the
#   B+/B0 lifetime ratio -- not a direct measurement, but the paper's own charge-conjugate
#   notation "B0 -> Ds- K0 l+ nu" is exactly the CDecay conjugate of anti-B0 -> Ds+ anti-K0 l- nu
#   used here, confirming this particle assignment (spectator d-bar -> anti-K0 instead of B+'s
#   spectator u-bar -> K+). Confirmed with the analysis author (2026-08-31).
# Responsible: Philipp Horak
# Email: phorak@uvic.ca
# Date: 20260831

Alias DsK0sig D_0*+
Alias anti-DsK0sig D_0*-
ChargeConj DsK0sig anti-DsK0sig

Particle DsK0sig      2.8 3.0
Particle anti-DsK0sig 2.8 3.0

Decay Upsilon(4S)
1.0 B0sig anti-B0sig  VSS_BMIX dm;
Enddecay

Decay anti-B0sig
0.500 DsK0sig  e-  anti-nu_e  PHOTOS LLSW 0.68 -0.2 0.3;
0.500 DsK0sig  mu- anti-nu_mu PHOTOS LLSW 0.68 -0.2 0.3;
Enddecay
CDecay B0sig

Decay DsK0sig
1.0 D_s+ anti-K0 PHSP;
Enddecay
CDecay anti-DsK0sig

End
